WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
The Object Detective: real Smithsonian CC0 objects, one fictional museum (the Lantern Museum)

2
00:00:03.001 --> 00:00:11.012
After hours at the fictional Lantern Museum: a short captioned intro, skippable

3
00:00:11.013 --> 00:00:13.514
Skip any cinematic from the first frame (Esc)

4
00:00:13.514 --> 00:00:18.517
Case 1: learn the tools on one real object from the Smithsonian's open-access collection

5
00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:24.018
Raking light shows tool marks, wear and repairs the flat view hides

6
00:00:24.018 --> 00:00:29.519
Magnify stamps and inscriptions; measure against the catalog record

7
00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:35.524
Case 2: is the museum's label right? Weigh real records and fictional documents

8
00:00:35.524 --> 00:00:41.027
Compare objects side by side, rate your confidence in each claim

9
00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:45.529
Then write a corrected label, and see it in the case

10
00:00:45.529 --> 00:00:50.538
Every decision also works in text mode, with no 3D needed

11
00:00:50.538 --> 00:00:55.043
Fictional documents are always labeled. Play free at immersive-learning-showcase.vercel.app
